SMART SWITCH BOARD — FRESH PWA FILES

Files:
- index.html
- manifest.json
- sw.js
- icons/icon-192.png
- icons/icon-512.png

IMPORTANT:
1. This is a new demo interface. Device quantities remain configurable.
2. Runtime switch states and timer end-times are stored in localStorage. Browser/phone time is used to calculate remaining time when the page reopens.
3. It is a simulation only; it does not control real electrical devices without a separate controller and safe hardware.
4. Upload the CONTENTS of this folder into the root of the GitHub repository, keeping the icons folder intact. Do not upload the outer ZIP as the site.
5. GitHub Pages should serve:
   https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/YOUR-REPO/manifest.json
   https://YOUR-USERNAME.github.io/YOUR-REPO/sw.js
6. After deployment, open the manifest URL and sw.js URL once, then in PWABuilder paste the site's base URL and press Start.
7. If PWABuilder still reports “Missing Name”, check that index.html contains:
   <link rel="manifest" href="./manifest.json">
   and that the live website shows the NEW index.html. The report can remain stale until the site deployment and re-test complete.
8. A grey Package for stores button may mean the report has not passed the requirements for that package or that the current report view is not ready. Re-test after deployment. Do not assume the APK is built until a downloadable package is provided.

Suggested GitHub upload:
- Repository: dnagar07860-wq/smart-switch-board
- Branch: main
- Destination: repository root
- Keep the icons/ folder and the three root files together.
